index 0000000..844b36c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/common/request-id/CODEMANIFEST
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+Annotations: |
+  Documents the request/correlation-id feature: an AsyncLocalStorage-backed store
+  that lets every layer of one HTTP request (guards, interceptors, controllers,
+  services) read the same request ID that Nest writes to the X-Request-Id
+  response header, without threading it through method signatures or parsing it
+  back out of the response. packages/core wires `createRequestIdMiddleware` onto
+  every HTTP adapter (Express and Fastify alike) as the first middleware run for
+  each request; application code only ever calls `getRequestId`.
+
+---
+
+"getRequestId() -> result: string | undefined":
+  location: request-id.storage.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Returns the request ID of the HTTP request currently being handled, i.e. the
+    same value sent back in the X-Request-Id response header. Returns undefined
+    when called outside of an HTTP request (e.g. during application bootstrap).
+    Public API, re-exported from @nestjs/common.
+
+"runWithRequestId(requestId: string, callback: Function) -> result: any":
+  location: request-id.storage.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Runs `callback` with `requestId` bound to the AsyncLocalStorage store for the
+    duration of the call (and any async work started within it), so nested calls
+    to `getRequestId` return this same value. Internal; only
+    `createRequestIdMiddleware` calls this.
+
+"createRequestIdMiddleware() -> result: RequestHandler":
+  location: request-id.middleware.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Builds the platform-agnostic (req, res, next) middleware Nest registers on
+    every HTTP adapter. Not part of the public API — re-exported only from
+    @nestjs/common/internal for packages/core to wire up automatically; never
+    called directly by application code.
+
+    Algorithm:
+    1. Read the inbound X-Request-Id request header (case-insensitively); if it
+       is missing or empty, generate a new one with the shared random-string
+       generator
+    2. Set the resolved ID as the X-Request-Id response header, so it is present
+       on every response — including error and not-found responses, since it is
+       set before routing/guards/interceptors run
+    3. Call `runWithRequestId` with the resolved ID and the middleware's next
+       callback, so the ID is available to every downstream handler via
+       `getRequestId`
+
+---
+
+Author: Goga
+CreatedAt: 26/09/17
+Description: |
+  Documents the request-id cell: a small AsyncLocalStorage-backed store plus the
+  middleware factory that packages/core's NestApplication.init() registers on
+  every HTTP adapter, giving every service the same request/correlation-id
+  response header and the same getRequestId accessor regardless of whether it
+  runs on the Express or the Fastify platform adapter.
